Alarm Clock

An Android alarm clock that makes you complete challenges before an alarm can be
dismissed: math problems, photographing an object (recognised on device), a memory game,
retyping a string, or repeating a sequence. An alarm can require several, in order, each
with its own difficulty. There is no snooze, and a ringing alarm cannot be switched off,
deleted or edited from the alarm list, or silenced by restarting the phone, until its
challenges are done. Auto-silence still applies.

It is a fork of DeskClock from the Android Open Source Project, ported from Soong to
Gradle. Upstream is no longer maintained. See NOTICE for attribution and LICENSE for the
Apache License 2.0 that covers both the original code and the changes.

Build with ./gradlew assembleDebug (JDK 21, Android SDK). The application ID is
com.ammar.deskclock, so it installs alongside Google's Clock.
